{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is located between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b7704971f948dedbc57b455aa1db6e465eb7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YXS = 20^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/2974399d3fa659839b3ea69b682e8e1ae3ce68ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ZYX = 50^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, what is the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fa850d4133abdf00d8198a3bc5d6ea59133eba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QZY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dda0ff0aa29ceb573af91f2c127398fd40e8b4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;);  defaultpen(TimesRoman()); defaultpen(linewidth(1bp));  size(175); pair P = (0,3); pair Q = (8,3); pair R = (0,0); pair SPoint = (8,0); pair X = (1147/1841*8,0); pair Z = (639/1841*8,3);   pair direction = dir(20); path line1 = X--X+20*direction;  pair Y = intersectionpoint(line1, SPoint--Q);  draw(P--Q); draw(R--SPoint); draw(Z--X--Y--cycle);  draw((319/1838*8,3+39/1838*8)--(379/1838*8,3)--(319/1838*8,3-39/1838*8)); draw((422/1838*8,39/1838*8)--(482/1838*8,0)--(422/1838*8,-39/1838*8));   label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,W); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,E); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,W); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,SPoint,E); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,S); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;,Z,N); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,E); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"138\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/640e993a4e92e2082d133ea9e865d4373d7e462c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   30^{\\circ}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   20^{\\circ}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   40^{\\circ}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   50^{\\circ}  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   60^{\\circ}  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"468\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw a ray parallel to segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> extending to the left from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be an arbitrary point on the ray distinct from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/5585c39c7e5a60808fd50db97092fa9150b12a63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;); import geometry;  defaultpen(TimesRoman()); defaultpen(linewidth(1bp));  size(175); pair P = (0,3); pair Q = (8,3); pair R = (0,0); pair SPoint = (8,0); pair X = (1147/1841*8,0); pair Z = (639/1841*8,3);   pair direction = dir(20); path line1 = X--X+20*direction;  pair Y = intersectionpoint(line1, SPoint--Q); real Yycoord = Y.y; pair T = (2,Yycoord);   real angleRadius = 20; markangle(&quot;&quot;, radius=angleRadius, Y, Z, Q, p=blue); markangle(&quot;&quot;, radius=angleRadius, Z, Y, T, p=blue); markangle(&quot;&quot;, radius=angleRadius, T, Y, X, p=red); markangle(&quot;&quot;, radius=angleRadius, SPoint, X, Y, p=red);       draw(P--Q); draw(R--SPoint); draw(Z--X--Y--cycle); draw(Y--(0,Yycoord));  draw((319/1838*8,3+39/1838*8)--(379/1838*8,3)--(319/1838*8,3-39/1838*8)); draw((422/1838*8,39/1838*8)--(482/1838*8,0)--(422/1838*8,-39/1838*8));   label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,W); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,E); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,W); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,SPoint,E); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,S); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;,Z,N); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,E); label(&quot;$T$&quot;,T,N); dot(T, black+2.5bp); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"138\" />\n</p><p>Then by alternate interior angles and the parallel segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/4839a63e46ca8e2cb9bad854ed077679cf363788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TY$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a9a59c6c4eec9b6138020641ce9b20fd9391b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QZY = \\angle ZYT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e125fc2069ea284b5292a100129ca13e1479cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YXS = \\angle TYX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4e6411e758811616dd93069bd9689a726dc03ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ZYX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f9216901643e8a12118deb487b5530f6d1f94f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ZYT + \\angle TYX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />, we can substitute these in:\n\\begin{align*}\n\t\\angle ZYX &amp;= \\angle ZYT + \\angle TYX\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\angle QZY + \\angle YXS\\\\\n\t\\implies \\angle QZY &amp;= \\angle ZYX - \\angle YXS\n\\end{align*}\nPlugging in the given angle values, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cbecb92e585d14ae564793154d5bfa8b4664acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QZY = 50^{\\circ} - 20^{\\circ} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 30^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"252\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 21 (page does not exist)\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 24 (page does not exist)\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"CEMC Cayley\">CEMC Cayley</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232230\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 198/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2054/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 314/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand siz